WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
And ai that keeps working for you, even after you close the app just launched. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 204. From there it's a deep dive on helpers that run without you. ChatGPT inside Chrome, and Meta's Muse app. And Thropic put out a research preview of Claude duet. The Dakota reports, and it is an agent rather than a regular chatbot. An agent is a helper that can take steps on its own, instead of waiting for you to type a question. A research preview means

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.420
this is an early test, more like a lab version than a finished school project.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.800
The system runs on cloud computers, machines and big buildings that stay on when your own

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.840
devices are off.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.480
Picture a really organized classmate working from a library you never visit, only texting

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.620
when they need a decision.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.660
Duet connects to outside services like Gmail, Slack, and Stripe, so it can schedule meetings

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.700
or prepare billing.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.820
It always asks for your approval before payments or sending messages.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:04.380
Bank transfers are blocked entirely, like a door that will not open no matter who knocks.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:10.100
The helper is built on Claude Opus 5.5, the model that does the thinking underneath.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.800
A model here is a trained system that learned patterns from a huge amount of text, then uses

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.840
those patterns to decide what to do next.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.480
It comes as a standalone app on Apple phones, on Android, and on Claude's website.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.220
Pro and Mac subscribers in the United States can join a wait list for access.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.880
Team and enterprise plans, the ones companies use, are not included yet.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:38.120
Every morning the agent sends a short summary of the most important items from connected apps.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.720
After that it only reaches out again when something needs attention.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.280
That morning ping is like a coach sliding a tiny game plan under your door,

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.560
then leaving you alone until the next play actually matters.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.280
users assign tasks by text or voice in a single ongoing thread.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.640
That thread can cover scheduling, dashboards, financial forecasts, prototypes, and web apps.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.300
One thread is like a group chat that never starts over, so the helper already knows the whole season.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.820
The agent works on its own virtual machine with a browser.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.840
A virtual machine is a computer made of software sitting in the cloud with its own screen and memory.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.220
Your laptop or phone does not need to stay powered on.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.760
It also reaches DocuSign and Shopify through more than 6,000 connectors and plugins from

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.820
the clawed marketplace.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.560
Connectors work like those little adapters in a charging drawer.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.660
Each one letting the helper plug into a different app.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.580
That is how it tracks unpaid invoices or gets payroll ready.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:42.440
For purchases, it uses Stripe Link with a virtual card, so your real card number is never

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:42.860
shared.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.240
Think of that virtual card as a single-use lunch ticket.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.520
The cafe sees the ticket, never your actual wallet.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:55.980
This setup responds to similar products from XAI with GrocBot in August, Metta with Muse

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.340
in September, and OpenAI with Dots in September.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.440
For a student, it could notice a project deadline in a connected calendar and send a reminder

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.500
without being asked.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.660
For someone running a small side project, it could watch for unpaid invoices while that

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:16.060
person focuses on the actual work. Right now, access is limited to the wait list for eligible

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:21.480
United States subscribers, and the agent still requires human approval on any risky step.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.740
You can join the wait list on Clawed's website if you have a qualifying plan,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:30.280
or open the regular Clawed app today, paste a list of your real deadlines,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.120
and ask it to plan a study schedule so you can see how multi-step tasks already feel.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:40.340
Leaving Minecraft running while you grab a snack is the closest everyday picture of this kind

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.778
of helper. The world keeps simulating rain, mobs, and daylight, even though your hands

00:03:45.778 --> 00:03:50.778
are off the keyboard. An agent gets that same kind of independence, but the world it

00:03:50.778 --> 00:03:55.838
tends is your mail, your calendar, and the jobs you already described. First, you connect

00:03:55.838 --> 00:04:00.518
the apps you actually use, and you talk in that long thread so it keeps memory of your

00:04:00.518 --> 00:04:05.558
preferences. Second, every few hours it walks through those apps the way you might skim

00:04:05.558 --> 00:04:10.498
your inbox between classes. Third, it sorts what can wait from what needs a human.

00:04:10.498 --> 00:04:12.958
Then, it only taps you for the human part.

00:04:13.478 --> 00:04:15.558
A normal chatbot is like a vending machine.

00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:18.438
Nothing happens until you walk up and press a button.

00:04:19.038 --> 00:04:23.398
The company's writing the rules still make it ask before anything risky, because one

00:04:23.398 --> 00:04:26.078
wrong automatic payment could wreck trust fast.

00:04:26.578 --> 00:04:28.638
The always on work is the computer's job.

00:04:29.178 --> 00:04:31.878
The safety rails are still written by people on purpose.

00:04:32.618 --> 00:04:37.098
Once you see it as a helper with a checklist and a locked wallet, the whole idea feels

00:04:37.098 --> 00:04:39.498
a lot more ordinary than the hype makes it sound.

00:04:39.498 --> 00:04:46.522
Open AI added chat GPT directly into Google Chrome, tech radar reports, so the chatbot

00:04:46.522 --> 00:04:48.562
can sit on the page you are already reading.

00:04:49.082 --> 00:04:52.762
You highlight text on any web page and ask about it without switching tabs.

00:04:53.462 --> 00:04:57.562
The integration lets the AI see the current page and answer questions about it right

00:04:57.562 --> 00:04:58.482
where you are browsing.

00:04:59.042 --> 00:05:03.342
You no longer have to copy and paste homework questions or research notes into a separate

00:05:03.342 --> 00:05:03.702
window.

00:05:04.302 --> 00:05:08.322
